A||||5||crzyone||Body panel removal||||1||
Z||000000||crzyone||03-09-2001||12:50 AM||||Hey there, I'm having problems removing my fastback clip.  Its all free as far as I can tell except for the top.  It seems to be attached to the roof.  Anyone have advice thats done this before?  Also, anyone have advice on how to remove the metal rivits holding on fenders?  <P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000001||crzyone||03-09-2001||12:51 AM||||I was also wondering how you remove the roof of the car, atleast the Fiberglass part.<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||03-09-2001||02:29 AM||||First you should get the chilton manual. On pages 10-13 thru 10-14 it shows detailed attachment points for these panels.<BR>You will have to take the inside trim loose by the seat belts and around the headliners because the head liner needs to come off. There are three nuts holding the top of the rear clip on and a bunch holding the roof panel on. The roof panel also has two in the cowl at the base of the windshield.  Don't forget the one by the seat belts (behind the trim) for the rear clip. Also you must remove the fuel door (I believe they are 7mm screws). To remove the latch, pry open the assembly at the seam. It will hinge open and the cable will pop out. The "windows" will stay attached to the clip (at least they do on the notch back). You have to take the roof loose to remove the rear clip, as it tucks underneath it.<P>The rivets are steel and should be drilled out with a 1/4 inch bit. Pain in the a$$ cause they like to turn. There is another steel rivet at the bottom of the fender hidden under the rocker panel. Good luck. I had to remove the whole rocker panel.... more steel rivets there.<P>Why are you doing this anyway?? Are you building a kit car or just transferring the body to another Fiero?  I am thinking of converting my notchback to a fastback this summer if I can find a good rear clip. Take pictures and let us know how it goes. Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg">   <BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000003||crzyone||03-09-2001||02:48 AM||||I'm replacing my rear clip. The previous owner had a rollover and beat it up pretty bad.  He did all the bodywork to repair it but I found a rear clip for $300 with the fastback windows still on it.  A place just outside of Edmonton puts Lambo kits on Fieros so I have a pretty good source for Fiero body and interior parts.   I'll have to pick up that manual, thanks for the advice!   Also, my 85SC gave up the ghost so its my new parts car for my GT.  I'm using the hood and roof, replacing every body panel that was damaged.    I'll take pics<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
